## Standing 9-point pre-flight (run before any code on any batch)

1. `git status` + `git log -1` — confirm tree state.
2. `pnpm --filter @orqafy/web test` — confirm 719/719 GREEN baseline.
3. Read input Zod schema of any router procedure the batch claims to reuse.
4. If router newly READS a field, verify all existing tests on that path mock the field.
5. Grep schema.prisma for any model in scope; confirm fields before scoping migrations.
6. Confirm package.json has any third-party library called out in scope.
7. Re-read .claude/rules/memory-governance.md §1 for the tier classification.
8. Emit explicit branch-creation line item in the BUILD BATCH PROPOSAL.
9. For publicProcedure vs protectedProcedure claims, grep the router to verify.

## Recurring-pattern lessons banked (apply at next batch PRE-FLIGHT)

- 🟢 publicProcedure tenant resolution — input.tenantSlug → db.tenant.findUnique;
  default warehouse server-side. NEVER let client supply warehouseId on public path.
- 🟢 System-actor lookup for guest writes — db.user.findFirst({isActive:true},
  orderBy:{createdAt:"asc"}) returns seeded webmaster for required createdById FKs.
- 🟢 Rate-limit tier — rateLimiters.public.check(ip) at 10/min/IP for guest mutations
  (NOT 30/min — actual config is 10).
- 🟢 sanitizePlainText on user-facing text fields before storage.
- ⚖️ Order-creation duplication tolerated — extraction deferred until 3rd variant.
- 🔴 useCart() shape gotcha — destructure mismatch caught at typecheck.
- 🟢 Intentional scope-trim — 5× consecutive (cart-only, order-only, Xendit-only,
  crypto-only, CRUD-only). Direction F COMPLETE 3/3 across 21a/b/c.
- 🟢 Helper-extract refactor pattern — protected→public dual-caller surfaces extract
  to src/lib/ helper.
- 🟢 RED-phase Zod-enum tightening — assert specific mock-side error marker + mock
  was-called to force true RED when new enum value would also Zod-reject.
- 🟢 Atomicity through in-transaction external calls — external HTTP inside DB
  transaction acceptable for payment surfaces.
- 🟢 As-any cast cleanup post-GREEN — grep `as any` after implementation; remove dead
  casts before lint flags them.
- 🟢 BUILT-IN NODE:CRYPTO SUFFICES — no need to add libsodium/tweetnacl for symmetric
  encryption. node:crypto + aes-256-gcm is FIPS-approved AEAD.
- 🟢 AES-256-GCM FORMAT — `{iv}.{authTag}.{ciphertext}` dot-separated base64url. IV
  12B per encryption (never reused), auth tag 16B mandatory.
- 🟢 LAZY ENV READ FOR TESTABILITY — getKey() reads process.env at CALL time, not
  module-import time. Tests manipulate env var per-test without vi.mock.
- 🟢 FILE-LEVEL RED — when test file imports not-yet-created module, vitest fails
  entire file at load. Still valid RED.
- 🟢 .env.example does NOT exist in this project. Skip it in future batches. Use
  .env.dev for runtime + CREDENTIALS.md for human-readable documentation.
- 🟢 LAYERING ADMIN-GUARD ON WRITEPROCEDURE — compose `writeProcedure.use(...)`
  to inherit demo-tenant block + add role check in one procedure surface. Avoids
  duplicating the demo logic across admin write procedures.
- 🟢 MASKED-DISPLAY PATTERN — never return *Enc fields. Return public-safe fields
  + has-value booleans (hasSecretKey, hasWebhookToken). Form inputs always start
  empty. User re-enters ALL secrets on every save. No partial update path in v1.
- 🟢 STATESYNC-FROM-QUERY VIA USEEFFECT — sync tRPC useQuery data to local form
  state via useEffect, NOT guarded-setState-during-render. StrictMode-safe.
- 🟢 XENDIT SDK TESTCONNECTION CONTRACT — `new Xendit({secretKey})`, then
  `xendit.Invoice.createInvoice({data:{externalId, amount, description, invoiceDuration}})`
  returns `{id, ...}`. `xendit.Invoice.expireInvoice({invoiceId})` voids it.
- 🟢 VERCEL-PLUGIN HOOK AS SELF-REVIEW REMINDER — even when skipping the skill
  load per Rule 28, the auto-suggestion fire prompts a useful pause for
  pattern-based self-review. Net positive on otherwise-skipped hooks.
- 🔴 [NEW from 21c] SCHEMA @@schema("public") IS NOT TENANT-SCHEMA-PER-TENANT —
  prior banked lesson called EcommerceOrder "tenant-schema-per-tenant" which was
  wrong. Public-schema entities with no tenantId column have NO TENANT ISOLATION
  AT ALL. The fix is to add tenantId, not to assume search_path handles it.
  Pre-flight check: grep `@@schema("public")` AND `tenantId` for each model in
  scope. If public-schema AND no tenantId AND multi-tenant feature needs tenant
  resolution → MIGRATION REQUIRED, not search_path trickery.
- 🟢 [NEW from 21c] WEBHOOK ENUMERATION PREVENTION — return same status code (401)
  for "unknown order" AND "wrong token" cases. Otherwise attacker can probe
  status-code differences to discover valid order IDs. Trade-off: legitimate
  Xendit webhook retries continue indefinitely on bogus IDs, but Xendit never
  sends bogus IDs in normal operation (it only webhooks for invoices YOU created).
- 🟢 [NEW from 21c] BUILD BATCH PROPOSAL OPTIONS PATTERN — when pre-flight surfaces
  a critical architectural gap not in .whatsnext, HALT before any code. Emit
  numbered options (A/B/C/D) with cost/benefit/tier per option. User picks.
  Don't ad-hoc-decide architecture mid-implementation. Direct application of
  Rule 29 (no fuzzy reasoning, ask if not in DECISIONS_LOG/PRODUCT.md/inputs.yml).

